## Product intent

For Avi and agents creating plans: make the intended user experience explicit before writing formal requirements. Preserve the requested outcome; surface omitted scenarios and unsupported additions early. Existing full verification is unchanged. Product shaping is advisory and enabled by default in authoring/read flows; it does not create a new approval gate or claim to machine-prove semantic intent.

Normal journey: read owner request/current product → record brief, scenarios, source/assumption distinctions → map scenarios to requirements and tasks → receive gap diagnostics and a reviewer brief → use existing review/activation process.
Recovery: absent or malformed shaping data is reported explicitly with an actionable authoring scaffold. Legacy plans remain usable.
Non-goals: external framework adoption, second spec store, automatic reinterpretation of owner speech, simulated reviewers, weakened verification, owner methodology questions, unbounded monitoring, unrelated frozen-test implementation.

