## Design

### Bar-to-work map for this plan

| bar | implementing plan items | evidence plane |
|---|---|---|
| R-1 | P-001, P-002 | tree |
| R-2 | P-001, P-003 | tree |
| R-3 | P-002, P-003 | tree |
| R-4 | P-004 | deployed |
| R-5 | P-002, P-003 | tree |
| R-6 | P-002, P-003 | tree |

Reuse: canonical plan Markdown persisted in the existing plan store; source-turn references; R-N/P-NNN/Decision identities; plan parser and source reader; existing authoring tools and activation consult/preview. No migration, new table, parallel spec store, recurring service or new verb. Extend plans:audit with an advisory shaping preview only if needed; existing activation/completion audits retain their semantics. Interpretive review uses the existing reviewer route and clearly distinguishes deterministic structural diagnostics from independent product judgment.

Shaping data contains: audience, current problem, intended outcome, non-goals, original source references, relevant facts/assumptions/decisions, scenarios with trigger/user action/expected outcome, applicable failure/recovery and boundary cases, and links to canonical requirement/implementation identities. Material choices are flagged; ordinary choices get recommended assumptions. A scenario's implementation details are separate from its intended behavior.

Testing: conventional Vitest unit tests for parsing, malformed and partial input, applicability, dangling mappings, source/assumption separation and reviewer context; tool-level tests verify the actual consumer path and legacy behavior. Exercise three representative feature ideas as maintained suite fixtures (bug report retry, notification preferences, collaboration permissions) and record a bounded comparison of shape omissions against an intentionally incomplete direct-spec draft. No invented improvements/accuracy rate and no claim of real owner benchmarking from fixtures. A future observational benchmark may be recorded as owned follow-up; it does not withhold a verified working authoring flow.

Acceptance: focused suites plus required checks; staging/current-build MCP route exercised for authoring/audit/read flows; final live MCP response tied to exact deployed SHA. Final-release item legitimately requires deployed main because its claim is shipment.

